WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:40.050
For many of the million and a half Catholics
in the United Arab Emirates it's the stuff

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.630
of dreams.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:47.020
The idea of the Pope visiting Arabian Peninsula,
the birthplace of Islam, was unthinkable a

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.530
few years ago.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.800
Pope Francis was invited by Abu Dhabi's rulers.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.289
Local Parish Priest Rheinhold Sahner says
the Pontiff wants to foster tolerance and

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:59.359
promote a moderate brand of Islam.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:03.679
It's definitely a signal that he wants to
build bridges.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:11.550
He wants to say, look, Islam is changing,
it can change and also wants to change.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:18.470
The Emirates have declared 2019 as the year
of tolerance - and there is a lot of symbolism

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.540
in the invitation.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:33.710
I am sure it will enhance the relationship
between different religions, it is a historic

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.400
visit.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.190
Pope Francis will be in the Emirates for three
days.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:42.590
He's expected to address a series of issues
including the lack of legal rights for foreign

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.730
workers.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:58.530
But the fact a Pope will lead a Catholic service
on the Islamic Arabian

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:52.220
Peninsula

00:02:52.220 --> 00:03:51.090
is

00:03:51.090 --> 00:04:02.810
a

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:46.790
sensation

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:48.310
in itself.

